%N A401795 Triangle read by rows: T(n,k) is the number of nonempty convex vertex sets with diameter k in the n-Fibonacci cube graph.
%C A401795 The n-Fibonacci graph is an induced subgraph of the n-hypercube graph, whose nonempty convex sets are the 3^n sub-cubes. The convex sets of the Fibonacci cube are the distinct subsets formed by the intersection of these sub-cubes with the graph. The resulting vertex sets are not necessarily complete cubes.
%C A401795 T(n,k) is the number of words of length n over the alphabet {0,1,2} avoiding the substrings 11, 21, 12 with k 2's.
%H A401795 Andrew Howroyd, <a href="/A401795/b401795.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..1325</a> (rows 0..50)
%H A401795 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/FibonacciCubeGraph.html">Fibonacci Cube Graph</a>.
%H A401795 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/GraphDiameter.html">Graph Diameter</a>.
%F A401795 G.f.: (1 + x - y*x^2)/(1 - (1 + y)*x - x^2 + y*x^3).
%e A401795 Triangle begins:
%e A401795    1;
%e A401795    2,   1;
%e A401795    3,   2,   1;
%e A401795    5,   5,   3,   1;
%e A401795    8,  10,   8,   4,   1;
%e A401795   13,  20,  19,  12,   5,   1;
%e A401795   21,  38,  42,  32,  17,   6,   1;
%e A401795   34,  71,  89,  78,  50,  23,   7,  1;
%e A401795   55, 130, 182, 180, 133,  74,  30,  8, 1;
%e A401795   89, 235, 363, 398, 331, 213, 105, 38, 9, 1;
%e A401795   ...
%o A401795 (PARI) row(n) = Vecrev([1,0,0]*([1,1,y; 1,0,0; 1,0,y])^n*[1,1,1]~)
%o A401795 (PARI) T(n) = {[Vecrev(p) | p<-Vec((1 + x - y*x^2)/(1 - (1 + y)*x - x^2 + y*x^3) + O(x*x^n))]}
%o A401795 { my(A=T(10)); for(i=1, #A, print(A[i])) }
